# Necromancy's 2022-12-08 ruling: it is sacrificed at the beginning of the next cleanup step only if it was cast using its own
# permission to be cast as though it had flash. With Valley Floodcaller on the battlefield ("You may cast noncreature spells
# as though they had flash"), two permissions let Bot1 cast it in Bot2's turn, a time a sorcery couldn't have been cast, and
# Bot1 chooses which one it casts it by (CR 601.3). Cast by Floodcaller's, no delayed sacrifice is made: Necromancy (a plain
# enchantment, with no creature card in any graveyard to return) is still on the battlefield in Bot1's next turn.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Valley Floodcaller
Sol Ring
Mox Jet
Necromancy
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Valley Floodcaller.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Necromancy.Cast
Bot1.Modes(Valley Floodcaller)
[T2 Bot2.End]
? Delayed.Count = 0
[T3 Bot1.Main1]

